{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":755566,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,4]],"date-time":"2026-05-04T20:39:27Z","timestamp":1777927167687,"version":"3.51.4"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>A critical gap exists in the understanding of the intrinsic deformation behavior of perfect single-crystal high-entropy alloys (HEAs) under extreme conditions, despite their importance as ideal models and for engineering applications. This study employs molecular dynamics simulations to systematically investigate the uniaxial tensile response of three representative FeCrNiCo-based HEAs:FeCrNiCoMn, FeCrNiCoAl0.3, FeCrNiCoAl0.5) at temperatures from 273 K to 900 K and strain rates of 1\u00d7[[EQUATION]]s\u22121 and 6\u00d7[[EQUATION]]. By analyzing stress\u2013strain curves, dislocation nucleation and evolution, and atomic-scale phase transitions, we reveal the coupled regulatory mechanisms of temperature, strain rate, and composition. All three single crystals exhibit pronounced temperature and strain-rate sensitivity: strength decreases linearly with temperature due to thermal softening, while higher strain rates impart significant strengthening. These findings provide essential atomic-level insights into the intrinsic deformation of FeCrNiCo-based HEAs, offering fundamental data for their application under extreme operating conditions.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6691661","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,1]],"date-time":"2026-05-01T22:36:42Z","timestamp":1777675002000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["\u200bAl content Driven Phase Transition and Dislocation Dynamics in Single-Crystal FeCrNiCo-based High-Entropy Alloys under Extreme Conditions\u200b"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"ruichen","family":"Dong","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Yongqing","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,1]],"date-time":"2026-05-01T22:36:42Z","timestamp":1777675002000},"score":39.32445,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=6691661"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.6691661","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,2]],"date-time":"2026-02-02T15:57:44Z","timestamp":1770047864553,"version":"3.49.0"},"reference-count":62,"publisher":"Informa UK Limited","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]],"date-time":"2025-10-21T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1761004800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["www.tandfonline.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Materials at High Temperatures"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,2]]},"DOI":"10.1080\/09603409.2025.2571840","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]],"date-time":"2025-10-21T16:18:57Z","timestamp":1761063537000},"page":"58-68","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1080\/tandf_crossmark_01","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Analysis of creep in class A alloys with dislocation climb based models"],"prefix":"10.1080","volume":"43","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8494-3983","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Rolf","family":"Sandstr\u00f6m","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","place":["Stockholm, Sweden"]}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"301","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_3_5_2_1","doi-asserted-b